---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Refinance Rate Lock (Timing and costs)";
const description =
  "What a refinance rate lock is, how long it lasts, and how to compare lock costs. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-01-31";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/refinance-rate-lock" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Rate lock</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Refinance rate lock: timing and cost tradeoffs</h1>
    <p>
      Rate locks can protect you from rate increases but may add cost or limit flexibility. This guide shows how to think about lock
      duration, cost, and timing.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/guides/refinance-checklist">Refinance checklist</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Break-even guide</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic hub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What a rate lock does</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      A rate lock holds a quoted rate for a set period. Longer locks can cost more or carry a higher rate. Make sure the lock covers
      the expected closing timeline.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to compare locks</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare the rate and fees with different lock durations.</li>
      <li>Ask about extension costs if closing is delayed.</li>
      <li>Confirm whether float-down options are available.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Questions to ask the lender</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Lock length and whether the rate is truly guaranteed.</li>
      <li>Extension fees and how many days each extension adds.</li>
      <li>Float-down pricing if rates improve before closing.</li>
      <li>What happens if the appraisal or underwriting is delayed.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Match lock length to your expected closing timeline.</li>
      <li>Include extension fees in your total cost estimate.</li>
      <li>Confirm whether float-down options are available.</li>
      <li>Recalculate if your closing date moves.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Target closing date and appraisal timeline.</li>
      <li>Lock fee or rate impact for each duration.</li>
      <li>Float-down rules and trigger conditions.</li>
      <li>Extension fee schedule if delays occur.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Choosing a lock that is too short for the closing timeline.</li>
      <li>Ignoring extension fees or relock costs.</li>
      <li>Comparing rates without including lock costs.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can I let a lock expire?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      You can, but you may lose the locked rate and face new pricing. Ask about extension policies.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Are longer locks always worse?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Not always. If a longer lock prevents an extension or rate increase, it can be worthwhile.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-checklist">Refinance checklist</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-closing-costs">Refinance closing costs</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/discount-points-vs-lender-credits">Points vs credits</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/guides/refinance-checklist">Refinance checklist</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic hub</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Break-even guide</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-01-31</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>



